#{[17592186313332 #edb/ref 1080 "-3.11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313332 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313332 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ad4efbe5-fdc7-5fd4-9d30-e094f70445a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313380 #edb/ref 1080 "2.00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313380 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313380 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b4624dcd-9d25-51e5-9616-19707034be81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313620 #edb/ref 1080 "7.11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313620 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313620 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d2678f8a-ed71-5433-86a0-c0296b22d487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314135 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314135 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314135 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186312340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314135 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2eaed716-9dc7-57e6-94cd-28e635420e6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314356 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314356 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314356 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314356 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186313327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314356 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "82387b89-5506-58bc-b197-21d516777f3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314869 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314869 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314869 #edb/ref 1069 "q-339858" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314869 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314869 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x+y,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with two steps to approximate $y(1)$ and $y(2),$ rounded to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314869 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47caf66e-659a-55c7-bd96-d84c0c91d3be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314869 #edb/ref 1074 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(2).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is $2,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-0}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((x+y)+({x}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y)+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(1)$ and $y(2).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y \\\\  & =0+1+3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=1,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y \\\\  & =1+2+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(1)≈1.00,\\,y(2)≈6.00.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{11}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04d2a009-9a40-5d25-99e2-4f97af963231" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b726bfa-ba4c-5d91-9f6d-6a3764d8755d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1594e17d-7011-5f7d-aa6a-12336ec25a8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321479 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321479 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321479 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b5f94c5-0d1b-5f79-944c-8cb9d821beed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321490 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{6}{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321490 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321490 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c533ee8-f9db-5f4a-a560-8035da471b44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921863