f 17592186045417] [17592186350824 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350824 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350824 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350824 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186350003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350824 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "46676d10-821d-5121-88ba-a5db1e61fc4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351222 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351222 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81106" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351222 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351222 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351222 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "820db9dd-f4cd-512d-b911-c52d62f6eb3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351222 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354757 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354757 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354757 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a1bc7b6-4de7-5eac-8417-854e3e18c590" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355774 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355774 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355774 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7da5b856-80e8-5cfd-bd82-d217ab37885e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355847 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355847 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355847 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8626180b-9f54-5542-bbda-3b519ffbbcb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356085 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356085 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356085 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a00f8753-5db0-5f2a-a18d-d3faa6c8c488" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356384 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356384 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356384 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c4d3dc9e-cb4f-5ec5-920b-00a0a9195ba2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186354757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186354757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357144 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7ee1fe3e-224e-55a4-98f8-d5e86ba6333e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357737 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357737 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357737 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357737 #edb/ref 1071 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=32t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+ϕ)+16t$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)+2t$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+8t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357737 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "91ea3a27-d7dd-5526-bebd-b64e4b8069b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357737 #edb/ref 1074 "The general solution is the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution:\n\n$$\ny(t)={y}_{c}(t)+{y}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$ It can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=16\\,⟹\\,\\omega =4.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ Since the external force is a linear function, we assume that the particular solution is also a linear function,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha t+\\beta .\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =2$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)+2t, \\\\ y(t) & =R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)+2t, \\\\ y(t) & =A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnly II matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357894 #edb/ref 1080 "0.27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357894 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357894 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1103e6c4-8e5a-5d60-a8d6-1e582b31d670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358408 #edb/ref 1080 "0.31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358408 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358408 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4beccc4b-bd42-53f7-a6ef-d29833929fbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358525 #edb/ref 1080 "0.16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358525 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358525 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "58efc89e-0bb9-5250-bf2e-d9981f1e00d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359833 #edb/ref 1080 "0.13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359833 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359833 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ea0097db-0220-5610-aa9c-bf8496bfb7cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359876 #edb/ref 1080 "0.23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359876 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186359876 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee51d506-3a45-567d-86d2-6491d5d72676" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186357894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186358525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186359876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186358525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360193 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "79790386-5ca3-5b7e-a326-b45ba6bd2fed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1071 "The time that a particular laptop battery lasts is normally distributed with a mean of $32$ hours and a standard deviation of $4$ hours. What is the probability that a full charge lasts for $36$ hours or more? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8413\\,$ | $\\,0.8438\\,$ | $\\,0.8461\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8643\\,$ | $\\,0.8665\\,$ | $\\,0.8686\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5563fda7-bd6a-55bd-869b-0a5d94077bb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360541 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $X$ represent the time the full charge lasts. Then we have $X∼N(32,{4}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(X\\ge 36).$ Thus, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 36) & =P(Z\\ge \\frac{36-32}{4}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 1) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n1-Φ(1)=1-0.8413≈0.1587.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a full charge lasts $36$ hours or more is approximately $0.16.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1080 "images/cd/cd1f754fa00d1af2d8901ecc4c0cac434afb433474685fe7777d74f1703bafb2.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361045 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2eeddbc3-0c2b-51c9-a0c9-e864cef13cda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361085 #edb/ref 1080 "I and IV only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361085 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361085 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36b8832f-f459-53a5-bebf-7fce914129df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361108 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c5/c5e335ffe5f2343671d1f9eca6cedc34ef34a9700837451e963cfcfe1cd153d5.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361108 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361108 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b5a1453-83df-5991-9fd6-135cf92a1272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361122 #edb/ref 1080 "images/eb/eb621888b04d5bd9b842624c278422995db44097adde61bbc769e8df0a5a47e7.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361122 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361122 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f0f0bcd-a732-5bb7-8af2-fe05f1453089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361243 #edb/ref 1080 "images/2d/2d352cf134fa7aa740d42f1de4e731cf9f53e26341a4ee3fefae809db0c8a3f1.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361243 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361243 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59405ea1-d578-52de-82ff-d38f4fd2dabb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361267 #edb/ref 1080 "images/a7/a77fcb19143b7bdee347993a1da4fb6f73c5c1460c55ecab24ffde9afe7f6cf0.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361267 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361267 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5f7dcf80-41db-5be0-ac2e-e22110ddadb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361274 #edb/ref 1080 "images/58/58efe73124a5f0fa8824ea05d118ea92ea1b30cf950f740c9c9b5376650044bd.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361274 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417]